course: dictionary
lesson: 139
title: Advise, advice and practise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To advise someone is to tell them what you think they should do. A friend might advise you to wear a coat. «Travellers to some countries need extra vaccines, and a travel nurse advises which ones.» The nurse tells people what they should have.
explain: Advise can also mean to tell people officially about something. «Passengers are advised to stay seated» is a message from the people in charge. It tells everyone what is safest to do.
explain: Watch the spelling. Advise, with an s that sounds like z, is a verb, a doing word. Advice, with a c that sounds like s, is a noun, a thing you are given. Practise, with an s, is also a verb, as in «I advise you to practise».
fact: Advise is a verb. Its forms are advises, advised and advising.
fact: «Advise» means to tell someone what you think they should do.
fact: «Advise» can also mean to tell people officially, as in «Passengers are advised to stay seated».
fact: «Advice» is a noun, a thing: «Take my advice.» Advice with c, practise with s: remember which is which.
fact: Patterns to learn: «advise someone to do something» and «advise against something». For example, RoSPA advises never going onto frozen ponds.
exercise: «Passengers are advised to stay seated.» What does advised mean here? | *Officially told what to do | Sold a ticket | Carried to their seats | Asked to sing a song
exercise: In «Take my advice», what kind of word is advice? | An adjective, a describing word | A verb, a doing word | A full stop | *A noun, a thing
exercise: «A travel nurse advises which ones.» What is the nurse doing? | Selling the medicines | Counting the people in the queue | Singing to the children | *Telling people what they should do
test: The sign says «Visitors are advised to keep away from the edge.» What does advised mean? | Shouted at loudly | Invited to a party | Given a present | *Officially told what is safe
test: Fill the gap with the noun: «Take my ___.» | advise | practise | advised | *advice
exam: Which sentence uses advise as a verb meaning to tell someone what they should do? | The advice from the nurse was very helpful | I need some good advice, please | *My teacher will advise me to read more every night | Her practice starts at six o'clock
